---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PadelScoreboardWidget from '../../components/PadelScoreboardWidget.astro';
import { breadcrumbs, webApplication } from '../../lib/jsonld';

const canonicalPath = '/sports/padel-score/';

const jsonLd = [
  webApplication({
    name: 'Padel Scoreboard',
    description:
      'Track a padel match point by point with sets, tie-breaks, golden point, serve indicator and a match timer.',
    path: canonicalPath,
  }),
  breadcrumbs([
    { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
    { name: 'Sports', path: '/sports/' },
    { name: 'Padel Scoreboard', path: canonicalPath },
  ]),
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Padel Scoreboard · Sets, tie-breaks and match timer"
  description="Track a padel match point by point: sets, games, tie-breaks, golden point, serve indicator, team names and a match timer. Share the score with a link. Free and browser-based."
  canonicalPath={canonicalPath}
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <nav class="text-sm text-zinc-500 dark:text-zinc-400" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
    <a href="/" class="hover:text-zinc-900 dark:hover:text-zinc-100">Home</a>
    <span class="mx-2">/</span>
    <a href="/sports/" class="hover:text-zinc-900 dark:hover:text-zinc-100">Sports</a>
    <span class="mx-2">/</span>
    <span>Padel Scoreboard</span>
  </nav>

  <h1 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:mt-4 sm:text-4xl">
    Padel Scoreboard
  </h1>
  <p class="mt-2 max-w-xl text-zinc-600 sm:mt-3 dark:text-zinc-400">
    Keep the score of a padel match, from the first point to the final set. Tap a
    team to add a point, follow the serve, and share the result with a link. Team
    names, colours and the match timer stay with you.
  </p>

  <div class="mt-6 sm:mt-8">
    <PadelScoreboardWidget />
  </div>

  <section class="mt-12 space-y-3 text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300">
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">How padel scoring works</h2>
    <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed">
      A game is first to four points: 0, 15, 30 and 40. At 40-40 the tool uses a
      golden point by default, so the next point wins the game. Switch to
      advantage scoring if your court plays the traditional way, where a team
      must win two points in a row from 40-40.
    </p>
    <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed">
      A set is first to six games with a two-game lead. At 6-6 the set goes to a
      tie-break to seven points, still with a two-point lead. A match is usually
      best of three sets; the tool also supports a single set, best of five and
      a stand-alone tie-break.
    </p>
    <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed">
      The serve alternates every game. In a tie-break the first server plays one
      point, then each team serves two points in turn. The team that received
      first in the tie-break serves first in the next set.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-10 space-y-3 text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300">
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">The match timer</h2>
    <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed">
      The clock starts when you record the first point. You can pause it at any
      time, and it stops by itself when the match ends. On a phone or tablet you
      can keep the screen on from the match settings, so the scoreboard stays
      visible between points.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-10 space-y-3 text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300">
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Sharing the score</h2>
    <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed">
      Copy match link puts the score in the URL fragment. The fragment is not
      sent to the server, so the score does not appear in request logs. It is a
      snapshot of the moment you copy it, not a live feed: copy a new link after
      the next point if you want to send an update.
    </p>
    <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed">
      Team names are left out by default. If you tick the box in the Share
      panel, the names travel in the link, where anyone who has it can read
      them. They may also appear in browser history or chat previews. The
      "Copy result" button gives you a plain text summary with the names, which
      is handy for a club chat.
    </p>
    <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed">
      The score and names are stored in this tab only. A reload keeps them,
      closing the tab clears them, and nothing is sent to a server.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-10 space-y-3 text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300">
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Common questions</h2>
    <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-sm leading-relaxed">
      <li>
        <strong>How many sets are in a padel match?</strong> Most matches are
        best of three. Some tournaments use best of five, and casual games are
        often a single set or a tie-break.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>What is a golden point?</strong> At 40-40 the next point wins
        the game. It is common in amateur padel and is the default here.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Who serves next?</strong> The team that did not serve the last
        game serves the next one. During a tie-break the rotation is one point,
        then two points each.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Can I correct a mistake?</strong> Yes. Undo removes the last
        point, and you can keep undoing back to the start of the match.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Does the timer keep running if I reload?</strong> Yes. The
        clock uses a saved start time, so it catches up when the page loads
        again.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
